# Architecture

## Layout

```
*.html                 # Public pages (index popup, class pages, memberships, …)
partials/              # Shared header/nav fragments
css/                   # Site + page styles
js/                    # Browser scripts (availability sync, anchors, header)
netlify/functions/     # Receiver webhooks + lib (popup rollover, managed tables)
tests/                 # node:test suites for sync/receiver logic
scripts/               # One-off measurement / maintenance scripts
```

## Placement

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Homepage popup markup / carousel | `index.html` + `css/popup.css` |
| Live popup/table rendering | `js/smartastro-availability.js` |
| Wall-clock display helpers | `js/smartastro-schedule-display.js` (+ Netlify twin) |
| `replaceWeek` merge / popup state | `netlify/functions/lib/smartastro-popup-rollover.js` |
| Managed table upsert / windows | `netlify/functions/lib/smartastro-managed-destinations.js` |
| Availability batch + removals | `netlify/functions/lib/smartastro-availability.js` + handler |
| Sticky-header hash offset | `js/anchor-offset.js` + `js/compact-header.js` |

## Boundaries

- Prefer structured sync state over hand-editing weekly class rows in HTML when SmartAstro manages the destination.
- Keep Netlify `lib/` free of browser DOM APIs; keep browser JS free of Node `fs` / Blobs.
- Match existing vanilla JS patterns — no framework without an explicit decision.
